//
// IDENTITY -- PROVED, not assumed. The retail W3DFunctionLexicon callback
// table is a 12-byte-stride array of {const char *name, void *fn, pad} at
// 0x012BA580. Its entry at 0x012BA5BC is {0x0111D37C, 0x00403D0A}; the string
// at 0x0111D37C is "W3DCommandBarHelpPopupDraw", and 0x00403D0A is a 5-byte
// ILT thunk whose `jmp` targets 0x0079C7E0. The three already-landed siblings
// resolve through the same table the same way (W3DCommandBarGenExpDraw ->
// 0x0042121F -> 0x0079B7D0, W3DCommandBarBackgroundDraw -> 0x004152D5 ->
// 0x0079CC00, W3DCommandBarForegroundDraw -> 0x00425437 -> 0x0079CD60), so the
// lift's name is confirmed by the binary, not by the lift. Arity agrees: the
// body takes exactly two stack words and returns with a bare `ret`.
//
// BFME DIFFERENCE FROM THE TWIN: only the image HEIGHT of the two end caps is
// read -- retail loads [image+0x28] for endBar/beginBar/centerBar and never
// touches [image+0x24], so the twin's getImageWidth() stores are gone. The
// clipping test is recomputed from the coordinates rather than reusing
// reg.hi.y, which is the shape the register allocator produced.
//
// FRAME (read from the /FAsc listing of this exact source, which matches
// retail displacement for displacement): with esp = E at the top of the else
// branch, pieces E-0x40, pos E-0x3c (x then y), size E-0x34, start E-0x2c,
// end E-0x24, IRegion2D reg E-0x20, EH record E-0x0c. `sub esp,0x34` plus
// four pushes. topSize/bottomSize/centerWidth are fully register-allocated
// and take no slot; the AsciiString temporary of the static image lookups
// shares the pieces slot, which is why pieces lands below pos.
//
// RESIDUE (8 bytes, 0.9905; blocker=regalloc). Exact size, 48 relocations,
// and probe reports shape 1.000 -- the whole difference is the order of two
// hoisted reloads, at +0x256/+0x25a and again at +0x2d9/+0x2dd:
//     retail  mov edi,[esp+0x18] ; mov edx,[esp+0x14]   ; pos.y then pos.x
//     ours    mov edx,[esp+0x14] ; mov edi,[esp+0x18]   ; pos.x then pos.y
// The register ASSIGNMENT is identical (pos.y=EDI, pos.x=EDX, size.y=ECX,
// start.x/size.x=EAX) and so is every other byte, including the tail of the
// function. Both sites are reload-only basic blocks entered from a block end
// (the loop back edge at 0x254 and the enableClipping call at 0x2d3), each
// with a second entry that skips the reloads (0x209 and 0x28c), so the order is
// the allocator's per-block range order, not a use order. The same two slots
// load pos.x-first at 0x1e6 and at 0x30f in BOTH builds, so it is not a
// global ordering rule.
//
// ALREADY TRIED AND MEASURED (do not repeat): tools/rotation_sweep.py, 31
// call-argument/copy toggles, 0 moved a byte; tools/alloc_residue.py reports
// the webs as identical-register reload swaps; tools/shape_family_levers.py
// over sib,register,bool,test,copy,store,loop,branch,constant,frame (11
// choices) driven by tools/shape_search.py, 121 trials, plateau at 0.9905, as
// did an earlier 300-trial run on a different choice set. By hand, all of
// these stayed at 8 or got worse: declaration order of pos/size, dead
// bottomEnd/topStart and range locals (the ZH twin's unused key points), for
// vs while vs do-while loop forms, scalar start/end in place of the ICoord2D
// pair, a separate clipWidth, hi.y-before-hi.x and lo.y-before-lo.x,
// aggregate `IRegion2D reg = {...}`, a nested block around the clip section,
// swapping every add()'s operands, reordering the two "draw end" blocks in the
// else branch, an explicit region pointer, &pos/&size taken through local
// pointers, a local centreBar height, splitting the guard into three ifs, and
// hoisting a local for the image-height used by the loop.
//
// These compact views expose only the offsets and virtual slots this body reads.
